\begin_layout Standard
Tables 123-126 in the online appendix erroneously excluded male respondents
 from the analytic sample and used unweighted observations.
 The corrected version uses household and village weights and uses all individua
l respondents.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Tables 88, 97, and 111 in the online appendix reporting the effects of male
 and female transfer recipients erroneously displayed results for monthly
 versus lump sum transfers.
 Table 104 in the online appendix for male and female transfer recipients
 erroneously displayed results for large verus small transfers.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The number of observations displayed in Tables 47, 54, 61, 68, 75, 82, 89,
 98, 105, 112, 119, 128, 135, 141, and 147 in the online appendix erroneously
 included participants receiving large transfer amounts.
 The correct number of observations is 1,244 for household level regressions,
 1,058 for households with school-aged children, 1,931 for individual level
 regressions, and 908 for regressions with female respondents.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Tables 37, 65, 72, 95, 102, and 132 in the online appendix erroneously omitted
 observations with missing outcome variables when calculating differential
 attrition rates for Lee treatment effect bounds.
 The corrected version includes the entire original sample.
